course: dictionary
lesson: 2424
title: The Cyrillic alphabet
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Cyrillic is an alphabet, a set of letters used to write a language. It can be an adjective, as in «Cyrillic letters», or a noun, as in the name of the alphabet itself. Context helps you here: «Ukrainian is written in the Cyrillic alphabet, which has 33 letters.»
explain: Some Cyrillic letters look like English ones but make different sounds. «Some Cyrillic letters look like English ones but stand for other sounds: В is v, Н is n, Р is r, С is s and Х is kh.» So do not trust your eyes alone. Check the sound.
explain: One Cyrillic letter can stand for two English letters. «One Cyrillic letter can stand for two English ones: Ш is sh, Ч is ch, Я is ya and Ю is yu.» When you meet a new letter, ask: what sound does it make in this word?
fact: Cyrillic is an alphabet, the set of letters used to write some languages.
fact: Languages written in Cyrillic include Ukrainian, Russian, Bulgarian, Serbian, Belarusian, Macedonian, Kazakh and Mongolian.
fact: Cyrillic was created long ago from Greek letters and is named after Saint Cyril, a missionary.
fact: Some Cyrillic letters look like English ones but have different sounds: Р is "r", Н is "n", С is "s" and В is "v".
fact: Ukrainian has special letters like Ї, Є and Ґ, which Russian does not use.
exercise: «Ukrainian is written in the Cyrillic alphabet, which has 33 letters.» What is Cyrillic? | A type of English grammar | A sound a cat makes | A kind of cheese made in Russia | *An alphabet, a set of letters used to write some languages
exercise: Which Cyrillic letter stands for the sound "n"? | *Н | Ж | Х | Р
exercise: «One Cyrillic letter can stand for two English ones: Ш is sh.» Which Cyrillic letter stands for "sh"? | Р | В | С | *Ш
test: Which languages are written in Cyrillic? | *Ukrainian and Russian | Spanish and Italian | French and English | Greek and Arabic
test: The Cyrillic letter С makes which sound? | *s | z | ch | k
exam: The Cyrillic letter Р looks like an English "P" but makes which sound? | v | p | sh | *r
